    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295p",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "295P Conditions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295p"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, do either or both of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine that all authorisations under the integrated public\nnumber database scheme are granted subject to specified\nconditions;\n\n(b) determine that a specified kind of authorisation under that\nscheme is granted subject to specified conditions.\n\n(2) An authorisation under that scheme is granted subject to any\ncondition specified in an instrument under this section that is\napplicable to that authorisation.\nNote 1:\nAn authorisation may also be granted subject to conditions imposed in\naccordance with that scheme: see section 295F.\nNote 2:\nSection 295R creates an offence for breaching a condition of an\nauthorisation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, do either or both of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine that all authorisations under the integrated public\nnumber database scheme are granted subject to specified\nconditions;\n\n(b) determine that a specified kind of authorisation under that\nscheme is granted subject to specified conditions.\n\n(2) An authorisation under that scheme is granted subject to any\ncondition specified in an instrument under this section that is\napplicable to that authorisation.\nNote 1:\nAn authorisation may also be granted subject to conditions imposed in\naccordance with that scheme: see section 295F.\nNote 2:\nSection 295R creates an offence for breaching a condition of an\nauthorisation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295p-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295p-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6390059a62c7bf59749b39b58c7b07a5853e69b556b214bbe96ca2c49b8ebe85"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295p",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "295P Conditions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, do either or both of\nthe following:\n\n(a) determine that all authorisations under the integrated public\nnumber database scheme are granted subject to specified\nconditions;\n\n(b) determine that a specified kind of authorisation under that\nscheme is granted subject to specified conditions.\n\n(2) An authorisation under that scheme is granted subject to any\ncondition specified in an instrument under this section that is\napplicable to that authorisation.\nNote 1:\nAn authorisation may also be granted subject to conditions imposed in\naccordance with that scheme: see section 295F.\nNote 2:\nSection 295R creates an offence for breaching a condition of an\nauthorisation."
    },
