    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "295S Remedial directions for breaching a condition",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295s"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA is satisfied that a person has\ncontravened, or is contravening, a condition of an authorisation in\nforce under the integrated public number database scheme.\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written direction requiring the\nperson to take specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene the condition, or is unlikely to\ncontravene the condition, in the future.\n\n(3) A person must not contravene a direction under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(5) A direction given under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA is satisfied that a person has\ncontravened, or is contravening, a condition of an authorisation in\nforce under the integrated public number database scheme.\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written direction requiring the\nperson to take specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene the condition, or is unlikely to\ncontravene the condition, in the future.\n\n(3) A person must not contravene a direction under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(5) A direction given under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295s-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "26fc2519813bb3a966f6e15384efce64d3947d207c50dea25e0ee6d940411860"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295s",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "295S Remedial directions for breaching a condition",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the ACMA is satisfied that a person has\ncontravened, or is contravening, a condition of an authorisation in\nforce under the integrated public number database scheme.\n\n(2) The ACMA may give the person a written direction requiring the\nperson to take specified action directed towards ensuring that the\nperson does not contravene the condition, or is unlikely to\ncontravene the condition, in the future.\n\n(3) A person must not contravene a direction under subsection (2).\n\n(4) Subsection (3) is a civil penalty provision.\nNote:\nPart 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty\nprovisions.\n\n(5) A direction given under subsection (2) is not a legislative\ninstrument."
    },
