    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295u",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "295U Report to Minister",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295u"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At the time the ACMA gives the Minister a report under section 57\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005,\nthe ACMA must give the Minister a separate report on the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the compliance by persons with authorisations granted under\nthe integrated public number database scheme;\n\n(b) any other matter relating to the operation of that scheme that\nthe ACMA considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to include in the separate report any\nmaterial:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of the separate report to be tabled\nin each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that\nHouse after the day on which the Minister receives the separate\nreport.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At the time the ACMA gives the Minister a report under section 57\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005,\nthe ACMA must give the Minister a separate report on the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the compliance by persons with authorisations granted under\nthe integrated public number database scheme;\n\n(b) any other matter relating to the operation of that scheme that\nthe ACMA considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to include in the separate report any\nmaterial:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of the separate report to be tabled\nin each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that\nHouse after the day on which the Minister receives the separate\nreport.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295u-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295u-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-295u-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a9d3ba03801b8e0dd367116a460a5db7058ac42b9b08fc0b010776c422ce0eb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-295u",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "295U Report to Minister",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At the time the ACMA gives the Minister a report under section 57\nof the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005,\nthe ACMA must give the Minister a separate report on the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the compliance by persons with authorisations granted under\nthe integrated public number database scheme;\n\n(b) any other matter relating to the operation of that scheme that\nthe ACMA considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The ACMA is not required to include in the separate report any\nmaterial:\n\n(a) that is of a confidential nature; or\n\n(b) the disclosure of which is likely to prejudice the fair trial of a\nperson.\n\n(3) The Minister must cause a copy of the separate report to be tabled\nin each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that\nHouse after the day on which the Minister receives the separate\nreport."
    },
