        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006-sch-1-sec-14-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0586f74f8e17bdbdfd209392b926611e72843b55baa3f064f083e5a95c5cdec6",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information is permitted for certain purposes during an exemption period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-amendment-integrated-public-number-database-act-2006#sch-1-sec-14",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "14 Telecommunications Amendment (Integrated Public Number Database) Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "No. 155, 2006\n\n(a) before the commencement of this item, information or a\ndocument was disclosed to a person as permitted by\nsection 285 of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and\n\n(b) the disclosure was for a purpose covered by subparagraph\n285(1)(c)(ii) of that Act.\n(2)\nDuring the exemption period, the person is taken, in relation to any\ndisclosure to the person:\n\n(a) of information or a document that satisfies paragraphs\n285(1A)(a) and (b) of that Act; and\n\n(b) that is for a purpose covered by subparagraph 285(1A)(c)(ii)\nof that Act;\nto hold an authorisation in force under the integrated public number\ndatabase scheme permitting the person to use and disclose the\ninformation or document.\n(3)\nIf:\n\n(a) within the exemption period, the person makes an\nauthorisation application under that scheme; and\n\n(b) the purpose for which the authorisation is sought is a purpose\ncovered by subparagraph 285(1A)(c)(ii) of that Act;\nthen, until the ACMA makes a decision on the application, the person is\ntaken, in relation to any disclosure to the person:\n\n(c) of information or a document that satisfies paragraphs\n285(1A)(a) and (b) of that Act; and\n\n(d) that is for the purpose for which the authorisation is sought;\nto hold an authorisation in force under that scheme permitting the\nperson to use and disclose the information or document.\n(4)\nIn this item:\nexemption period means the period of 28 days beginning on the day on\nwhich this item commences.\nintegrated public number database scheme means the scheme in force\nunder section 295A of the Telecommunications Act 1997."
    },
